      "claim": "L4 records for lipophilic basic amines—imipramine (100% human oral absorption, essentially complete within 80 min), diphenhydramine (>90% human absorption; Caco-2 A-to-B ~39 x10^-6 cm/s), chlorpromazine (96% human absorption; high Caco-2 Papp), promethazine (A-to-B ~23 x10^-6 cm/s), and chlorprothixene (Papp 18 x10^-6 cm/s)—show that the query's structural class (lipophilic weak base with tertiary amine) is associated with high intestinal absorption and permeability.",
